WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.310
In the Summer of 2007, in the heart of a forest
in Northern California, hundreds of people

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.780
were gathered for a yearly art and music festival.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.920
It was meant to be a celebration, a weekend
filled with creative expression, dancing,

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.350
and, sure, probably some illegal substances.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.710
But it was all set to be a mostly wholesome
affair and one that the attendees had been

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.200
looking forward to all year.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.039
On the evening of the festival’s first night,
after a day of painting, performance art,

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:35.980
interpretive dance, and folk-pop fusion, the
organizers put together a massive bonfire.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.281
Everyone gathered around, roasting marshmallows
and vegan hot dogs, and breaking out their

00:00:40.281 --> 00:00:42.610
acoustic guitars for a sing-along.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:47.739
It was all going well, and they were heading
into the third refrain of Kumbaya, when a

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:51.940
group of friends adding logs to the fire noticed
something odd.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:56.300
Some of the flames at the edge of the fire
pit were moving in a different direction than

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.300
the rest.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.059
While most of the flames flickered upward,
some tilting slightly with the direction of

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:07.000
the wind, these flames were moving sideways
against the wind, stretching themselves out

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.470
toward the grass.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:13.540
It seemed bizarre, impossible, and they wondered
at first if perhaps the brownies they had

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.479
eaten earlier had more than just chocolate
in them.

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:21.530
But then, the flames kept moving, taking on
a familiar shape.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:26.720
They were dancing orange and yellow flames,
there was no doubt about that, but they also

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.710
seemed almost like…fingers.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.240
The fingers extended outward, grasping for
something.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.470
Attached to the fingers was a hand, then an
arm.

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:41.920
Another hand joined it, fingers twisting into
the grass, which dried and crackled at its

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:42.920
touch.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:47.450
One of the friends, a young woman named Flower,
attempted to alert one of the event staff,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.790
but they were too busy trying to get their
marshmallow to the perfect shade of golden

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:51.790
brown.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:57.619
Unable to get any help, she watched helplessly
as the fiery hands dragged a head, a torso,

00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:00.689
and the rest of a humanoid body behind them.

00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:05.229
It looked like the shape of an ordinary man,
with the glaring exception that it was made

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:07.650
entirely out of fire.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:12.610
It stepped out of the fire pit, and began
to take slow, halting strides toward the gathered

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.610
crowd.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.160
Now, everyone took notice of what was happening.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.930
First, they froze in shock, staring at this
being of pure flame, unbearable heat radiating

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.870
off of him as he moved closer and closer.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.840
When he reached out a hand toward Flower,
and the arm of Flower’s dress ignited in

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.060
flames on contact, the first scream broke
through the silence.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.319
When they marketed this year’s event as
“Burning Man in the woods” this was not

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:38.970
what they had in mind.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.640
But there he was, just the same, a man made
of flames tearing through what was meant to

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.269
be a peaceful and happy event with no dangers
beyond exhaustion, dehydration, and maybe

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:51.880
a noise complaint or two.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.720
Instead, the crowd scattered in every possible
direction, running for their lives.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:02.390
It was already late for poor Flower, who fell
to the ground shrieking in agony as the fire

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:08.420
engulfed the organic material of her dress,
and the flaming man pulled her into its deadly

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.420
arms.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.620
Her screams went quiet, drowned out by the
crackling roar of the fire as it fed on her

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.440
flammable body.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:22.019
Once Flower was nothing but a pile of bones
and ashes, the entity began to walk slowly,

00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:25.560
purposefully, through the woods with its arms
outstretched.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.280
It brushed its fingertips over everything
it passed, every tree, every stump, every

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.450
plant or scrap of fabric torn off on a branch.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.049
The fire began to spread like, well, wildfire.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:40.730
By the time the first festival-goers made
it out of the forest and into the nearest

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:47.100
town to get help, dozens of acres of forest
were ablaze and over 50 people were dead.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.870
The fire department was deployed to the forest,
where they were able to contain the blaze

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.560
after hours of work.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.080
Meanwhile, word of the man made of fire that
destroyed the art and music festival reached

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:02.689
the only people qualified to deal with such
a creature: The SCP Foundation.

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:06.769
They deployed operatives embedded in the local
police force, who joined the fire department

00:04:06.769 --> 00:04:09.450
under the guise of providing reinforcements.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:14.030
Once the blaze was contained and the area
was largely safe to enter, they followed the

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:18.600
path of the fire and tracked the being responsible
for all of the destruction.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:23.639
They found it, shrunk to the size of a small
child, huddled in the fire pit where it all

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:26.960
began as if it was hiding from the fire hoses.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.910
Then, they apprehended the being later designated
SCP-457.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:38.460
SCP-457 is comprised of unknown materials,
though obviously it is made up of something

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.460
flammable.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.710
Whatever it is, it is made up of something
invisible and impossible to detect by any

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.930
known scientific means.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.400
The only visible aspect of the entity is the
flames it produces, which tend to make up

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.780
a humanoid shape as long as it has enough
fuel to reach that size.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.810
If it does not have enough fuel, it shrinks
in size, becoming as small as the single flame

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:01.540
atop a lit match.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:06.440
In its smallest form, it is indistinguishable
from any other small flame, except for the

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:11.889
occasional display of independence such as
jumping to other fires or flammable materials,

00:05:11.889 --> 00:05:14.070
which it can then use to grow larger.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:20.020
When it is large enough to take on a human
form, SCP-457 displays human-like intelligence

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:24.910
and is capable of communicating through writing
- which it does by burning letters into surfaces

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:28.630
with its flames - or even through speech.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:34.000
Though it lacks the anatomy to produce a traditional
voice, it produces coherent sounds via pressurized,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.770
superheated air as well as the crackle of
its flames.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:42.440
If provided with enough fuel to grow beyond
humanoid size, the entity can split into two

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.419
or more beings, depending on how much fuel
it is given.

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:52.830
However, this split state does not last, as
the separate instances of SCP-457 will attempt

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.259
to attack each other until they are the only
one left standing.

00:05:57.259 --> 00:06:02.590
SCP-457 seems to want nothing more than to
consume more and more fuel and spread as far

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.650
as it can.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:08.400
It has shown a troubling ability to learn
and adapt, purposefully breaking and interfering

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:12.830
with sprinkler systems in the building and
setting up elaborate traps for personnel it

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.080
does not like.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:19.700
Dr. Smythe, head of the research team assigned
to SCP-457, conducted an interview with the

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:24.199
subject on a rare day when it was feeling
cooperative, in order to better assess its

00:06:24.199 --> 00:06:26.240
psychology and motivations.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.770
Dr. Smythe entered SCP-457’s containment
chamber, carrying a fire extinguisher in case

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:34.280
of any hostility on the part of the entity.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.700
He stood on the other side of the blast shielded
window, for extra protection.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.860
It crackled pleasantly in the corner, seeming
to welcome him inside.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.240
He asked if it was capable of, or willing
to speak.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:47.720
It answered yes.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.050
He asked it how it felt about being confined.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.380
It responded plainly: “Dislike.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.380
No fuel.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.380
No Air.”

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:59.280
When Dr. Smythe reminded the entity that it
had enough air and fuel to survive, it argued

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.350
that it could not burn, and had no fuel.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:06.550
To clarify, Dr. Smythe asked, “Are you saying
that you cannot grow?”

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:12.050
At this question, SCP-457 moved back and forth
through a small section of the room, as if

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.270
pacing and looking for something.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.220
It said, “Grow.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.220
Need.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:21.639
Must grow,” and when asked how it felt,
it simply said: “Hungry.”

00:07:21.639 --> 00:07:25.980
As the questioning continued, the entity approached
the window and stretched a hand made of flame

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.330
toward the glass.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.110
For a moment, it stopped responding to Dr.
Smythe.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:34.800
In order to get the being’s attention back,
he casually brought up the subject of water.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:40.620
At the very mention of it, SCP-457 let out
a high-pitched scream and pressed itself against

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.389
the window in a threatening gesture.

00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:47.419
Dr. Smythe warned that it must move away from
the window, or it would be doused in water.

00:07:47.419 --> 00:07:53.479
It moved back, but screamed and hissed for
several more minutes, offended and upset.

00:07:53.479 --> 00:07:58.500
SCP-457 resumed its pacing, at a more aggressive
speed and intensity.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:00.750
All the while, it repeated: “Want fuel.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.840
Want air.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:02.940
Want burn.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:03.940
Want to burn.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:04.940
Want to burn.”

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:08.560
Again and again, getting louder and louder
as it moved.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.449
Dr. Smythe was perplexed by this behavior,
noting that there was no way out and wondering

00:08:13.449 --> 00:08:15.539
what it could be trying to accomplish.

00:08:15.539 --> 00:08:18.480
At this point, the interview took a turn for
the disastrous.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:24.389
Somehow, SCP-457 was able to damage the sprinkler
system and a section of the fuel injector

00:08:24.389 --> 00:08:27.759
that had been providing it with a small stream
of fuel.

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:32.390
With the nozzle broken open, several gallons
of gasoline came flooding out, allowing the

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:37.860
entity to grow to an incredible size in a
sudden, massively destructive blast.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:42.610
Exploiting a weakness in the blast shielding,
SCP-457 was able to escape its containment

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:46.980
for several minutes, burning its way down
the hall of the facility until the larger

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:50.850
sprinkler system activated, sending it hissing
back to its cell.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:56.090
There, it was apprehended by a team of guards
and herded into a new, higher-security cell.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:09:00.970
It is unknown how exactly the entity became
aware of the weaknesses in its containment

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:06.920
chamber, but this incident revealed that it
is a highly intelligent being capable of problem-solving.

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:11.779
However it learned this information, and figured
out how to exploit it, the Foundation realized

00:09:11.779 --> 00:09:15.980
that more extensive measures would have to
be taken to keep it locked down and keep the

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:18.000
general population safe.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.420
Due to the dangerous nature of SCP-457’s
corporeal form, highly specialized containment

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:26.800
procedures have been put in place to keep
the flame from spreading.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:31.560
The entity is kept in a 5 by 5-meter chamber
with at least nine inches of fireproofing

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.950
in place, including asbestos and perlite.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:39.610
The observation window is blast-proof and
resistant to extremely high temperatures.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:44.230
The room’s opening is made up of temperature-controlled
and airtight chambers that can be sealed in

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:46.160
the event of an escape attempt.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.370
The room itself is kept at a high humidity
level and has a drain installed on the floor,

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:56.350
with a sprinkler system in the ceiling and
emergency hoses that can be operated if additional

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.580
water is needed.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:02.920
A small portion of the room is free from water,
but only enough so that SCP-457 can maintain

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.220
its shape and protect itself from moisture.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:11.649
Any personnel that enter SCP-457’s containment
unit must wear Class-A temperature-controlled

00:10:11.649 --> 00:10:15.400
and flame-resistant suits, and must enter
in groups of three.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:20.970
Two of the three members of each group must
be armed with blast shields and fire extinguishers.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:25.040
Personnel are not permitted to enter the containment
chamber for any reason other than providing

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:30.250
daily fuel or fixing any issues with the room
or its sprinkler system.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:36.329
In some ways, its containment procedures are
reminiscent of a particularly spicy variant

00:10:36.329 --> 00:10:37.519
of SCP-173.

00:10:37.519 --> 00:10:41.830
If the entity attempts to attack any personnel,
it can be deterred via the application of

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:45.420
fire extinguishers or hoses until it backs
down.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:50.089
If it escapes from containment, further sprinkler
systems will be activated throughout the facility

00:10:50.089 --> 00:10:52.070
in order to contain the fire.

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:56.950
The highest priority, aside from keeping the
entity contained, is keeping it fed.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:01.720
Because it needs constant fuel in order to
survive, the Foundation is currently prioritizing

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.790
finding an infinitely renewable source of
fuel.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:10.800
Though many have been proposed, including
the use of other SCPs such as SCP-2689 and

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.850
SCP-124, no source has been officially approved
yet.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:21.130
In the meantime, they keep the burning being
fed and happy, or as happy as it can be.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:25.570
It will never be truly satisfied until a day
arrives when it can be permitted to spread

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:31.060
as far and wide as it wishes, to burn and
feed and engulf everything in sight.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:36.140
Let’s all hope that day never comes, but
if you start to feel unusually hot, if the

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:40.820
walls seem to suddenly blacken around you,
and you hear the final crackles before the

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:45.779
hissing tongues of flame lick at your bubbling
skin...Well, by that point, it’ll already

00:11:45.779 --> 00:11:46.779
be too late.

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:53.980
Now go check out “THIS SCP DOES NOT EXIST
- SCP-3930 - The Pattern Screamer” and “SCP-173

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:59.770
Origin Story - How 173 Got to Site-19” for
more strange and usual SCP’s!

